<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03Y1">Corollary <span data-tag="03Y1">7.1.4.35</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category, let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0 \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a reflective subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, and let $K$ be a simplicial set. If $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ admits $K$-indexed limits, then $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0$ also admits $K$-indexed limits. If $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ admits $K$-indexed colimits, then $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_0$ also admits $K$-indexed colimits. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Variant <a data-tag="04JX" href="/tag/04JX">7.1.4.33</a> with Corollary <a data-tag="04JW" href="/tag/04JW">7.1.4.29</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
